.po 1i
.TH SWITCH 1C UCB
.V 08/15/84 17:06:46
.\"@[$]switch.1C	1.5	08/15/84 17:06:46 - Zilog Inc.
.ad
.SH NAME
switch \- C Shell flow control statement for decision-making
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBswitch \fI(string)\fR
.sp
	\fBcase \fIlabel1:\fR
.sp
		\fIcommand\fR
.sp
	\fBbreaksw\fR
.sp
	\fBcase \fIlabel2:\fR
.sp
		\fIcommand\fR
.sp
	\fBbreaksw\fR
.sp
	\fBdefault\fR
.sp
		\fIcommand\fR
.sp
\fBendsw\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBSwitch\fR is generally useful in the context of a
\fIforeach\fR or \fIwhile\fR statement.
.PP
Each \fIcase label\fR is successively matched against the specified
\fIstring\fR. 
.PP
The file metacharacters "\ \fB*, ?, [, \fRand\fB ]\fR\ " can
be used in the \fIcase labels\fR.
If none of the \fIlabels\fR match before a \fIdefault label\fR
is found, the execution begins after the \fIdefault label.\fR
.PP
Each \fIcase label\fR and the \fIdefault label\fR
must appear at the beginning of a line.
The command \fBbreaksw\fR
causes execution to continue after the \fBendsw.\fR
Otherwise, control falls through case labels and default labels,
as in C.
If no label matches and there is no default, execution continues after
the \fBendsw.\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
break(1C),
breaksw(1C),
continue(1C),
exit(1C),
foreach(1C),
if(1C),
logout(1C),
while(1C).
.br
\fIThe C Shell\fR in the ZEUS Utilities Manual
